WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.206 --> 00:00:01.230
(soft music)

00:00:01.230 --> 00:00:03.140
- [Narrator] This month,
Tesla plans to release

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.479
a major upgrade to its driver
assistance software FSD-beta.

00:00:06.479 --> 00:00:10.840
That upgrade is expected
to extend public access

00:00:10.840 --> 00:00:14.283
to a feature intended to help
vehicles navigate cities.

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:18.530
Despite its name, FSD
or full self-driving,

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.950
still doesn't make cars fully autonomous

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:22.540
and Tesla instructs drivers

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:25.700
to remain alert with
their hands on the wheel.

00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:29.800
- Tesla began selling a
driver assistance package

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.710
that it calls full self-driving capability

00:00:32.710 --> 00:00:34.970
about five years ago.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:38.470
And so this feature
that's expected to help

00:00:38.470 --> 00:00:43.470
drivers navigate in cities
is part of that package.

00:00:44.580 --> 00:00:46.690
- [Narrator] This expands
upon Tesla's existing

00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:49.210
FSD system of driver assistance tools

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:51.450
that were designed mainly for highways.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:54.120
- Tesla has taken an unusual approach

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:57.920
to rolling out access to this upgrade.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:01.520
A small group of users has been testing

00:01:01.520 --> 00:01:04.900
this city-driving
feature for quite a while

00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:07.860
and using it on public roads,

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:11.920
often recording videos
of those experiences

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.640
and posting them.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:17.330
- Ooh, okay, wow.

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:18.880
That was awesome.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:23.440
- [Rebecca] That has helped
to drum up a lot of interest

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:26.620
and also invited scrutiny as well.

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.920
- [Narrator] Tesla owners
can buy full self-driving

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:32.160
for $10,000 or use it
through a subscription

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:34.660
of up to $199 a month.

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.060
But the wider public
hasn't been granted access

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.940
to the city-driving tool yet.

00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.020
Tesla has been preparing to release

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:43.980
its city-driving tool beyond
that small group of people

00:01:43.980 --> 00:01:45.950
who have been testing the software.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:48.330
Drivers have now been able
to request the feature,

00:01:48.330 --> 00:01:51.970
but CEO, Elon Musk, said they
would only be granted access

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:54.880
after having their
driving habits evaluated.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.610
- Tesla has said it's
taking into consideration

00:01:57.610 --> 00:02:01.830
a variety of factors, including
things like hard breaking

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.440
or aggressive turning.

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.680
And it's using those inputs to come up

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:12.200
with a safety score that will be used

00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:15.060
to prioritize who gets access.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:19.120
Tesla plans to release this upgrade

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:22.630
to drivers progressively
around a thousand a day

00:02:22.630 --> 00:02:24.630
based on their safety score,

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:27.770
but it remains unclear what happens

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.190
if you get caught in this space

00:02:30.190 --> 00:02:33.520
where Tesla doesn't think
you're driving is good enough.

00:02:33.520 --> 00:02:34.900
- [Reporter] The Tesla crushed

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:37.030
after slamming into an overturned semi.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:40.450
- A Bay Area Tesla driver
was playing video games

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.690
at the time of a deadly crash.

00:02:42.690 --> 00:02:44.270
- [Narrator] Tesla's latest upgrade

00:02:44.270 --> 00:02:46.380
comes in the wake of a series of crashes

00:02:46.380 --> 00:02:47.450
that have heightened scrutiny

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:50.010
of the company's driver
assistance software.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:52.960
- The new chair of the National
Transportation Safety Board

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:57.790
has been critical of Tesla's
driver assistance systems,

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:01.330
and really, specifically the language

00:03:01.330 --> 00:03:06.130
that the company uses
to describe its tools,

00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:11.130
but the agency doesn't
have regulatory authority.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:13.060
This really is a space

00:03:13.060 --> 00:03:16.200
that is not tightly regulated in the US

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:21.200
and so automakers have a
wide degree of latitude.

00:03:22.783 --> 00:03:24.370
(soft music)

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.280
- [Narrator] Tesla's
driver assistance software

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:27.930
comes in two bundles.

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:30.070
Autopilot comes as a standard system

00:03:30.070 --> 00:03:34.020
on new vehicles and primarily
assist highway driving.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:36.070
The second package is what Tesla calls

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:37.990
its full self-driving capability,

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.950
which is essentially an upgrade
that adds more features,

00:03:40.950 --> 00:03:44.600
but it's only available to
customers who buy the package.

00:03:44.600 --> 00:03:46.510
- Tesla drivers have identified

00:03:46.510 --> 00:03:47.920
a variety of tricks to make

00:03:47.920 --> 00:03:50.690
autopilot believe they
are focused on the road

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:54.610
even if they are literally
asleep at the wheel.

00:03:54.610 --> 00:03:56.590
- [Narrator] For years,
Tesla's faced criticism

00:03:56.590 --> 00:04:00.120
from some lawmakers about its
driver assistance software.

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:01.850
- You can take a water bottle,

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:05.660
take an orange and put it
right into the steering wheel.

00:04:05.660 --> 00:04:08.100
And then that tricks the system

00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:11.120
to believing that your
hands are on the wheel.

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:13.430
- [Narrator] Last month, the NTSB launched

00:04:13.430 --> 00:04:15.550
an investigation into a fatal crash

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:18.000
involving a Tesla vehicle in Florida.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:19.880
And in August, the National Highway

00:04:19.880 --> 00:04:21.730
Traffic Safety Administration said

00:04:21.730 --> 00:04:24.810
it was investigating
Tesla's autopilot system.

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:28.870
- But it's likely going
to take quite a while

00:04:28.870 --> 00:04:32.570
for that investigation to play out.

00:04:32.570 --> 00:04:35.550
We're just in the early stages.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:36.830
- [Narrator] In recent months,

00:04:36.830 --> 00:04:39.260
even Musk has expressed mixed views

00:04:39.260 --> 00:04:41.430
about the full self-driving system.

00:04:41.430 --> 00:04:44.310
- [Elon] We need to make
full self-driving work

00:04:44.310 --> 00:04:46.850
in order for it to be a
compelling value proposition.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:51.530
Otherwise, people are kind
of betting on the future.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.540
I mean, right now, it doesn't make sense

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:56.600
for somebody to do FSD subscription.

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.310
I think it's debatable.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:00.820
- [Narrator] Tesla did not respond

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.825
to a request for comment.

00:05:02.825 --> 00:05:05.242
(soft music)

